---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the Force Multiplier review website handles contact information, hosting and local interaction data."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap">
    <h1>Your information,<br />handled plainly.</h1><p class="lead">
      This page describes the GitHub-hosted website review preview.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section-bottom">
    <div class="prose privacy-copy">
      <h2>Contact information</h2><p>
        The contact page creates an email draft on your device or lets you copy your inquiry. It
        does not submit the form fields to a website backend. Sending the draft through your email
        app shares that message with Force Multiplier and the email providers involved.
      </p><p>
        Please avoid sending sensitive personal information in an initial inquiry. If you contact
        us, we use the information you provide to understand and respond to your request.
      </p><h2>Website hosting</h2><p>
        This preview is hosted by GitHub Pages. GitHub may process technical information, such as IP
        addresses, to provide and secure the hosting service. See <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          >GitHub’s privacy statement</a
        > for its practices.
      </p><h2>Analytics and cookies</h2><p>
        This preview does not install advertising trackers, analytics scripts or website cookies. It
        does not store inquiry fields in browser storage. Your email app and browser have their own
        settings and behavior.
      </p><h2>Questions or requests</h2><p>
        Contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with questions about information you
        have shared with Force Multiplier.
      </p><h2>Before production launch</h2><p>
        The production privacy information will be reviewed when hosting, inquiry delivery and any
        analytics are configured.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
